return [
  'beagle-dog-breed'=>'The beagle is a small to medium scent hound bred in England to hunt rabbits. Beagles stand up to 13 or 15 inches tall, weigh about 20 to 30 pounds, live 12 to 15 years and are cheerful, gentle with children and easy to groom — but vocal, food-driven and ruled by their nose.',
  'beagle-lifespan'=>'Most beagles live 12 to 15 years, and the AKC gives the breed a life expectancy of 10 to 15 years. Keeping a beagle lean is the biggest thing an owner can do for a long life, along with daily exercise, yearly vet checkups, dental care and a secure fence or leash.',
  'beagle-colors'=>'Beagles can be any true hound color. The classic tricolor — black saddle, tan head and white legs — is the most common, followed by red and white, tan and white and lemon and white. Chocolate, blue and true black and white beagles are rarer, and ticking can give a bluetick look.',
  'lemon-beagle'=>'A lemon beagle is a purebred beagle with pale yellow-cream and white coloring instead of the classic tricolor. Lemon puppies are born almost completely white and darken over their first months. They share the same temperament, size and health as other beagles and shouldn’t cost more.',
  'pocket-beagle'=>'A pocket or mini beagle is a beagle bred smaller than the breed standard, usually 7 to 12 inches tall. It isn’t a recognized variety, and breeding for tiny size can bring back, joint and dental problems. If you want a small beagle, a healthy 13-inch beagle is the better choice.',
  'do-beagles-shed'=>'Yes, beagles shed a moderate amount all year, with heavier shedding in spring and fall. Their short double coat is easy to manage: brush once or twice a week with a rubber curry brush, more in shedding season. Beagles are not hypoallergenic, so they don’t suit people with dog allergies.',
  'how-to-find-a-beagle-breeder'=>'A reputable beagle breeder health-checks the parents, raises puppies at home, keeps them until at least 8 weeks old, provides vet records, a microchip and a written health guarantee, and gives you a contract. Avoid sellers who want gift cards or crypto, add surprise fees or won’t answer questions.',
  'beagle-adoption-vs-breeder'=>'Adopting a beagle costs about $100 to $500 and gives an adult dog a home, but its background is often unknown. Buying from a breeder costs more, about $800 to $2,500, and gives you a puppy with known parents, health records, a written guarantee and lifetime support. Both are good choices.',
  'beagle-puppy-care'=>'In a beagle puppy’s first month, keep a calm routine: four small meals a day, potty breaks every one to two hours, crate training from day one, a vet visit within the first few days and gentle socialization. Beagle-proof your home first — they explore with their nose and mouth.',
  'beagle-mix-breeds'=>'Popular beagle mixes include the Beagador (Labrador), Doxle (Dachshund), Cheagle (Chihuahua), Bagle Hound (Basset Hound), Puggle (Pug), Bogle (Boxer), Beagi (Corgi) and Poogle (Poodle). Mixes can inherit any traits from either parent, so size, coat and temperament vary, even within one litter.',
  'beagle-lab-mix'=>'A beagle Lab mix, or Beagador, is a cross between a beagle and a Labrador Retriever. Beagadors usually weigh 25 to 50 pounds, live 10 to 15 years and are friendly, playful, food-loving family dogs that need at least an hour of exercise a day and shed moderately to heavily.',
  'dachshund-beagle-mix'=>'A Dachshund beagle mix, or Doxle, is a cross between a beagle and a Dachshund. Doxles usually weigh 15 to 30 pounds and live 12 to 15 years. They are brave, curious, vocal and stubborn, and many inherit the Dachshund’s long back, which needs protecting from jumping and extra weight.',
  'beagle-chihuahua-mix'=>'A beagle Chihuahua mix, or Cheagle, is a small cross that usually weighs 9 to 20 pounds and lives 12 to 16 years. Cheagles are loyal, lively and often vocal, and tend to bond closely with one person. Early socialization helps, and they are sometimes sold misleadingly as “pocket beagles”.',
  'beagle-basset-hound-mix'=>'A beagle Basset Hound mix, or Bagle Hound, is a cross between two scent hounds. Bagle Hounds usually weigh 30 to 55 pounds and live 10 to 15 years. They are gentle, easy-going and vocal, with long ears that need weekly cleaning and a longer back that benefits from staying lean.',
  'beagle-boxer-mix'=>'A beagle Boxer mix, or Bogle, is a cross between a beagle and a Boxer. Bogles usually weigh 30 to 60 pounds and live about 10 to 13 years. They are playful, loyal and energetic family dogs that need at least an hour of exercise a day and early, consistent training.',
  'corgi-beagle-mix'=>'A Corgi beagle mix, or Beagi, is a cross between a beagle and a Corgi. Beagis usually weigh 20 to 35 pounds and live 12 to 15 years. They are smart, alert and energetic, often long-bodied and short-legged, shed quite a lot and may inherit a herding dog’s urge to nip at heels.',
  'beagle-training'=>'Beagles are smart and very food-motivated, so short, positive, treat-based sessions work best. Start potty and crate training on day one, practice recall on a long line, reward walking beside you, and teach a “quiet” cue. Most beagles should stay on a leash outside fenced areas.',
  'best-dog-food-for-beagles'=>'The best dog food for a beagle is a complete and balanced food for their life stage, from a reputable maker, fed in measured portions. Feed puppies three to four meals a day and adults two, keep treats under 10% of calories, and adjust portions to keep a visible waist.',
  'fat-beagle'=>'A healthy adult beagle usually weighs under 20 pounds (13-inch) or about 20 to 30 pounds (15-inch). If you can’t easily feel the ribs or see a waist, your beagle is overweight. Measure meals, count treats, walk daily and aim to lose 1% to 2% of body weight a week.',
  'hunting-with-a-beagle'=>'Beagles were bred to hunt rabbits and hares by scent, following the trail and announcing it with their bay so hunters can follow. A good hunting beagle is driven, steady and vocal. Most hunters introduce puppies to rabbit scent early and start field work between about four and eight months.',
  '13-inch-vs-15-inch-beagle'=>'Beagles come in two recognized sizes measured at the shoulder: 13 inches and under, usually under 20 pounds, and 13 to 15 inches, usually 20 to 30 pounds. Both have the same personality. A 13-inch beagle suits smaller homes; a 15-inch beagle is sturdier for active families.',
  'beagle-growth-chart'=>'Most beagles reach their adult height by about 12 months and fill out to their adult weight by around 18 months. A typical 8-week-old beagle weighs 2 to 5 pounds, a 6-month-old 9 to 18 pounds, and an adult up to about 20 pounds (13-inch) or 20 to 30 pounds (15-inch).',
  'are-beagles-good-apartment-dogs'=>'Beagles can live happily in apartments if their needs are met. Their small size and easy coat suit apartment life, but they are loud, need at least an hour of exercise a day and dislike being left alone. A 13-inch beagle, daily walks and company make apartment life work.',
  'are-beagles-good-with-cats'=>'Most beagles get along very well with other dogs and many live happily with cats, especially when raised together. Small pets such as rabbits, guinea pigs and hamsters are risky, because beagles were bred to hunt rabbits. Introduce pets slowly and supervise them closely at first.',
  'do-beagles-bark-a-lot'=>'Yes, beagles are one of the more vocal breeds. They bark, howl and bay — a hound cry bred to tell hunters where the pack is. Daily exercise, mental games, company and training a “quiet” cue keep the noise manageable, but a beagle will never be a silent dog.',
  'how-much-exercise-does-a-beagle-need'=>'Most adult beagles need at least an hour of exercise a day, split into two or more sessions, plus time to sniff. Puppies need short sessions — about five minutes of structured exercise per month of age, once or twice a day — and seniors need gentler, shorter walks.',
  'rescued-beagles'=>'Beagles are the dog breed most used in laboratory research, and thousands have been rescued in recent years. In spring 2026, about 1,500 beagles were released from Ridglan Farms in Wisconsin to shelters nationwide, and in 2022 around 4,000 were removed from an Envigo facility in Virginia.',
  'bi-ge-quan'=>'比格犬（Beagle，台湾称米格鲁）是源自英国的嗅觉猎犬，肩高不超过13或15英寸，体重约9至14公斤，通常能活12到15年。比格犬性格开朗、对孩子温和、容易打理，但爱叫、贪吃，而且鼻子主宰一切。',
  'are-beagles-good-family-dogs'=>'Yes, beagles are good family dogs for most homes. They are gentle, playful and patient with children, get along with other dogs and are easy to groom. They also bark and howl, steal food, follow their nose and dislike being alone, so they suit families who are home often.',
  'male-vs-female-beagle'=>'Male and female beagles differ only a little. Males are often slightly larger and more playful for longer; females often mature a little sooner and can be a bit more independent. Both are friendly and good with children, so an individual puppy’s personality matters more than sex.',
